  "text": "CDC Consumer Guide: Common Cold Prevention and Self-Care | Publisher: Centers for Disease \nSymptom Timeline and Clinical Evaluation\nCold symptoms typically improve within 7 to 10 days. When to Call a\nDoctor: - Symptoms that worsen or fail to improve after 10 days. - Severe\nor unusual symptoms, such as sudden high fever or severe chest pain. -\nSymptoms in individuals at high risk for flu complications.\nPage 2 of 4 | Official Educational Resource",
